# UNSLOP: interface and copy rules

Apply these rules to every interface file and every piece of text a person will read. The full handbook is under `{{SKILL_DIR}}/references/`, behind a deep index. Never read whole chapters: ask the index, then read only the line ranges it prints.

```sh
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/find.py --task pricing          # reading list for a kind of task
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/find.py focus ring on a button  # best sections for any question
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/find.py --text "draft copy"     # banned words in a draft, with replacements
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/find.py --tasks                 # every task route
```

Without Python, search `{{SKILL_DIR}}/references/DEEP-INDEX.md`: one line per section with its line range.

Before you finish a task, run the checks on the files you changed and fix what they report:

```sh
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/scan.py path/to/changed/files
python3 {{SKILL_DIR}}/scripts/lint.py path/to/file.md
```

Report the output. Never claim compliance you did not check.

{{CORE}}

